\section*{Chessboard from FEN}

This is an example of a chessboard generated from a FEN (Forsyth-Edwards Notation) string using \LaTeX.

\begin{center}
    % Set the board state using the FEN string
    % This FEN represents the starting position
    \newgame
    % You can replace this FEN string with any valid FEN position
    \setchessboard{
        showmover=false,
        boardlayout=normal
    }

    % Render the chessboard using the current state
    \chessboard[fen=rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1]
\end{center}

\end{document}
```

### Explanation of the packages used:
- **`chessboard`**: This package provides highly customizable commands for rendering chessboards, allowing you to change the size, colors, and margins of the board.
- **`skak`**: This is a standard package for typesetting chess games and parsing chess notation, including FEN strings.

To display a custom position, simply replace the FEN string inside the `\chessboard[fen=...]` command with your desired FEN notation.

